//! JSON Parser Library for Kira
//! A pure functional JSON parsing, manipulation, and serialization library.
//!
//! This library has been modularized into the following submodules:
//!
//! ## Module Structure
//!
//! - `json.types` - Core types (Json, JsonField, JsonError, Schema types) and type predicates
//! - `json.parser` - Parsing functions (parse, parse_strict, parse_bytes, parse_with_limits)
//! - `json.serializer` - Serialization functions (stringify, stringify_pretty)
//! - `json.transform` - Transformation functions (set_field, remove_field, merge, map_values)
//! - `json.equality` - Equality comparison (equals)
//! - `json.path` - Path-based access (get_path, set_path, has_path, remove_path)
//! - `json.builder` - Builder pattern and convenience constructors
//! - `json.schema` - Schema validation (validate, schema_*)
//! - `json.decode` - Typed deserialization (required_*, optional_*, DecodeError)
//! - `json.encode` - Typed serialization (encode_*, encode_field, encode_object)
//!
//! ## Usage
//!
//! Import specific functions from the relevant submodules:
//!
//! ```kira
//! import json.types.{ Json, JNull, JString, JNumber, JArray, JObject, JsonError, InvalidUtf8, is_string, as_string, get_field }
//! import json.parser.{ parse, parse_strict, parse_bytes }
//! import json.serializer.{ stringify, stringify_pretty }
//! import json.transform.{ set_field, remove_field, merge }
//! import json.equality.{ equals }
//! import json.path.{ get_path, set_path, has_path }
//! import json.builder.{ builder, with_string, with_number, build, json_null, json_string }
//! import json.schema.{ validate, schema_type, schema_object }
//! import json.decode.{ required_string, required_int, optional_bool, DecodeError, format_decode_error }
//! import json.encode.{ encode_string, encode_int, encode_object, encode_field, encode_array, encode_optional_field, collect_fields }
//! ```
//!
//! ## Quick Reference
//!
//! ### Types
//! - `Json` - The main JSON value type (JNull, JBool, JNumber, JString, JArray, JObject)
//! - `JsonField` - Key-value pair in an object
//! - `JsonError` - Structured error type with variants (InvalidUtf8, UnexpectedEof, etc.)
//! - `Schema` - JSON Schema for validation
//!
//! ### Parsing (String Input)
//! - `parse(string) -> Result[Json, JsonError]` - Parse JSON string
//! - `parse_strict(string) -> Result[Json, JsonError]` - Parse with duplicate key rejection
//! - `parse_with_limits(string, ParseLimits) -> Result[Json, JsonError]` - Parse with resource limits
//!
//! ### Parsing (Bytes Input - for untrusted external data)
//! - `parse_bytes(Bytes) -> Result[Json, JsonError]` - Parse with UTF-8 validation
//! - `parse_bytes_strict(Bytes) -> Result[Json, JsonError]` - Strict parsing with UTF-8 validation
//! - `parse_bytes_with_limits(Bytes, ParseLimits) -> Result[Json, JsonError]` - With resource limits
//!
//! ### Serialization
//! - `stringify(Json) -> string` - Compact serialization
//! - `stringify_pretty(Json) -> string` - Pretty-printed with 2-space indentation
//!
//! ### Type Checking
//! - `is_null`, `is_bool`, `is_number`, `is_string`, `is_array`, `is_object`
//! - `as_string`, `as_number`, `as_int`, `as_bool`, `as_array`, `as_object`
//!
//! ### Access
//! - `get_field(json, key) -> Option[Json]` - O(1) field lookup
//! - `get_index(json, index) -> Option[Json]` - Array access
//! - `get_path(json, "path.to[0].value") -> Option[Json]` - Path-based access
//!
//! ### Modification
//! - `set_field(json, key, value) -> Json` - Set/update field
//! - `remove_field(json, key) -> Json` - Remove field
//! - `merge(a, b) -> Json` - Shallow merge
//! - `merge_deep(a, b) -> Json` - Deep merge
//!
//! ### Validation
//! - `validate(json, schema) -> Result[void, List[SchemaError]]` - Validate against schema

module json

